From a4ee60c6ba6b81ac03135fc152a623700c2bb096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:47:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(simview): camcraft-sim check judges a 3-axis G-code file
 headless

Add the crate crates/simview (package camcraft-simview) with the binary
camcraft-sim. It has no edge to camcraft-app or camcraft-ui.

- `camcraft-sim cl <file.cl> ...` is the old sim-crate binary, moved
  with the same arguments, output and exit codes.
- `camcraft-sim check <file.nc> --stock <box> --tools <T map>
  (--post <.cps> | --dialect <name>) [--machine <.mch>] [--wcs G54=x,y,z]
  [--fixture <box>] [--cell <mm>]` parses the program with
  camcraft-gcode and runs:
  - the post manifest checks (kind served, programUnits, workOffsetMax);
  - the stock check (a rapid through the material that is left);
  - the holder law (shank and holder bands against that material);
  - the fixture law (verify's region-free laws over --fixture boxes);
  - the machine limits (#2585, in program coordinates);
  - the machine-part collision on the generated model (#2584).
- Exit 0: each check ran and passed. 1: bad input. 2: a check failed,
  with its NC line. 3: a check was not judged, named.
- A/B/C words refuse by name (the gcode parser). An unmapped T and a
  .camtools library refuse by name (#4465 follows up the library).

The decision files carry the #2574 research decisions with the crate
edges, and the unattended decisions of this slice.

Fixes #2586

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
